# BarberPro AI Insights — Cursor rules
1. Use Next.js 16 App Router (React 19) with strict TypeScript and define explicit types for page props, API payloads, and domain models.
2. Keep React UI components focused and move reusable displays into `/components` and business calculations into `/lib/business`.
3. Validate every external request with Zod and return structured HTTP errors without leaking internal diagnostics.
4. Read authentication from the Supabase server session and verify workspace membership before any tenant-owned read or write.
5. Enable PostgreSQL Row Level Security for each tenant-owned table and write tests proving cross-tenant requests fail.
6. Keep OpenAI keys and elevated Supabase credentials in server-only environment variables and never expose them to the browser or Git.
7. Derive product prices and commission rates on the server and record monetary amounts using integer centavos or exact decimal arithmetic.
8. Make sale creation atomic and idempotent using unique request keys and transactional PostgreSQL operations.
9. Use Vercel AI SDK only from a protected server route, send minimal aggregate metrics, and validate structured AI output before rendering.
10. Add Vitest tests for new business rules, API authorization and AI parsing, and run lint, typecheck, tests and build before merging.
